SCENE TIMING (0.0–15.0s)


P0 — Start Fight (0.0–0.3s)
Sharp energy ignition ping;
Both fighters, the Mech and the Kid charged, debris levitating, neon strobing violently.

P1 — Energy Burst Break (0.0–0.6s)
The tiny “ignition ping” explodes into a violent radial burst, hurling dust, debris, droplets outward.
Camera whip-zooms between their faces as the shockwave tears the neon reflections apart.

P2 — Instant Dash Clash (0.6–2.2s)

Kid FLASH-steps forward leaving afterimages.
Mech counters with a palm-blast lunge.
Camera tracks sideways, capturing sparks, puddle vapor, concrete chips flying.

Their punches collide mid-air with a bright plasma bulb.

P3 — Aerial Throw (2.2–3.7s)

Mech GRABS the kid and hurls him upward.
Camera cranes up with him as he spins through drifting neon-glass fragments.
Heat from the mech’s hand glows on the kid’s visor.

P4 — Wall Run Counterattack (3.7–5.0s)

Kid rebounds off a vertical wall, running sideways anime-style.
Camera tracks parallel, capturing pavement and neon signs streaking below him.
He launches down with a glowing dive-kick.

P5 — Shockwave Stomp (5.0–6.2s)

Mech STOMPS the ground before impact.
Ground cracks open—fracture lines glowing pink from internal mech energy.
Kid is thrown upward by the shockwave, debris orbiting him in slow-mo.

P6 — Drone Intercept Swarm (6.2–7.8s)

Kid’s drones snap into formation, spiraling around him like a shield.
Camera orbits fast.
Drones catch the mech’s beam, splitting it into refracted neon streaks that scorch the alley walls.

P7 — Kid’s Phase-2 Burst (7.8–9.5s)

Kid punches the air, releasing a massive spherical energy pulse.
Air bends; dust spirals inward; rain vaporizes.
Camera shakes violently; neon lights go dark from the EM surge.

P8 — Mech Punisher Charge (9.5–11.0s)

Through smoke and flickering neon, the mech CHARGES — faster than before.
Camera low to ground, tracking its massive steps, puddles exploding in heavy sprays.

It swings a huge arm with plasma coils streaking.

P9 — Counter Flashstep (11.0–12.2s)

Kid disappears for a frame (flashstep), reappears behind the mech.
Camera whip-pans with motion blur smears and neon trails.
He lands a back-kick that dents the mech’s spine plating.

P10 — Alley Collapse (12.2–13.4s)

The mech’s weight + energy ruptures the alley floor—
Concrete collapses into a glowing crater.
Camera drops with debris as smoke rises in volumetric pillars.

P11 — Final Power Standoff (13.4–15.0s)

Both combatants at crater edge, glowing with second-phase power.
Kid’s visor glyphs spinning like turbines, gloves vibrating with charge.
Mech’s eye blazing and lens rings spinning at max speed, sparks dripping.
Loose debris floats between them in slow spirals.

Camera push-in → EMP flicker → hard cut on bright white energy bloom.